<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_TarredSurgery_RecipeUsers.xml     SUMP_TAR_NASTINESS_1

  Attaches RUT_ScrubTarred to every race that can be operated on at all.
  Identical shape and reasoning to src/RimStarWars/BrainWorms/Patches/
  BrainWormSurgery_RecipeUsers.xml (read in full before writing this):
  vanilla attaches surgeries like ExciseCarcinoma through each race
  ThingDef's own <recipes> list, not through RecipeDef.recipeUsers, so
  "already lists ExciseCarcinoma" is the reliable marker for "this is a
  body a surgeon works on." Patches run against the raw XML before def
  inheritance resolves, so matching the two defs that DECLARE that list —
  Human (Races_Humanlike.xml) and the abstract AnimalThingBase
  (Races_Animal_Base.xml) — reaches every vanilla race through inheritance,
  and reaches any alien race in the load order that copied the vanilla list
  rather than inheriting it.

  Animals match too. Harmless: an animal never carries RUT_Tarred without
  first carrying RM_Filth_Tar (RM_MapComponent_CarriedFilthHediffLink reads
  Pawn_FilthTracker the same way for every pawn on the map, humanlike or
  not), and Recipe_RemoveHediff.AvailableOnNow returns false whenever the
  hediff is absent — the bill simply never appears on a clean animal's
  operations tab.

  ⚠️ A patch that matches nothing logs nothing. If "scrub off tar" is
  missing from a race's operations tab, this xpath found no <recipes> on
  it; add that race explicitly rather than assuming the patch ran.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[recipes/li="ExciseCarcinoma"]/recipes</xpath>
    <value>
      <li>RUT_ScrubTarred</li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
